      hu: "Changzhou, a Jiangsu tartomÃ¡nybeli Jangce-deltÃ¡ban fekvÅ‘ vÃ¡ros, jÃ³lÃ©tÃ©rÅ‘l Ã©s kulturÃ¡lis hagyomÃ¡nyairÃ³l ismert. TÃ¶bb mint 2500 Ã©ves mÃºltjÃ¡val Changzhou a Sui-dinasztia Ã³ta a Nagy-csatorna egyik fontos Ã¡llomÃ¡sa volt, ami elÅ‘segÃ­tette gazdasÃ¡gi nÃ¶vekedÃ©sÃ©t. A vÃ¡ros ma a fejlett gyÃ¡rtÃ¡s egyik vezetÅ‘ kÃ¶zpontja, kÃ¼lÃ¶nÃ¶sen a robotika Ã©s az Ãºj energiÃ¡k terÃ¼letÃ©n. Changzhout gyakran 'SÃ¡rkÃ¡nyvÃ¡rosnak' nevezik, itt talÃ¡lhatÃ³ a Tianning-templom, amelynek pagodÃ¡jÃ¡t a vilÃ¡g legmagasabb fapagodÃ¡jakÃ©nt tartjÃ¡k szÃ¡mon. Modern lÃ¡tvÃ¡nyossÃ¡ga a China Dinosaurs Park, egy hatalmas vidÃ¡mpark, amely a vÃ¡rost a csalÃ¡dos turistÃ¡k kedvelt cÃ©lpontjÃ¡vÃ¡ tette. A hagyomÃ¡nyos kÃ©zművessÃ©g, mint pÃ©ldÃ¡ul a finom changzhoui fÃ©sűk, tovÃ¡bbra is a helyi identitÃ¡s fontos rÃ©sze. Changzhou sikeresen Ã¶tvÃ¶zi tÃ¶rtÃ©nelmi csomÃ³pontkÃ©nt betÃ¶ltÃ¶tt szerepÃ©t a technolÃ³gia-orientÃ¡lt jÃ¶vÅ‘kÃ©pÃ©vel.",
      ro: "Changzhou, situat Ã®n Delta Fluviului Yangtze Ã®n provincia Jiangsu, este un oraș cunoscut pentru prosperitatea sa și tradițiile culturale bogate. Cu o istorie de peste 2.500 de ani, Changzhou a fost un popas important pe Marele Canal Ã®ncÄƒ din timpul dinastiei Sui, ceea ce i-a impulsionat creșterea economicÄƒ. AstÄƒzi, orașul este un centru de top pentru producția avansatÄƒ, Ã®n special Ã®n roboticÄƒ și energii noi. Changzhou este adesea supranumit 'Orașul Dragonului' și gÄƒzduiește Templul Tianning, a cÄƒrui pagodÄƒ este consideratÄƒ cea mai Ã®naltÄƒ pagodÄƒ din lemn din lume. Un punct de atracție modern este China Dinosaurs Park, un parc tematic imens care a conferit orașului reputația de centru turistic pentru familii. Meșteșugurile tradiționale, cum ar fi pieptenii fini din Changzhou, rÄƒmÃ¢n o parte vitalÄƒ a identitÄƒții locale. Changzhou Ã®mbinÄƒ cu succes rolul sÄƒu de nod istoric cu viziunea sa asupra unui viitor orientat spre tehnologie.",
      en: "Changzhou, situated within the Yangtze River Delta in Jiangsu Province, is a city distinguished by its enduring prosperity and deep cultural heritage. With a history spanning over 2,500 years, Changzhou became a vital stop along the Grand Canal during the Sui Dynasty, which catalyzed its economic development. Today, the city is a premier hub for advanced manufacturing, leading in sectors such as robotics and renewable energy. Often called the 'Dragon City,' Changzhou is home to the Tianning Temple, featuring a pagoda widely recognized as the tallest wooden pagoda in the world. A major modern attraction is the China Dinosaurs Park, a massive theme park that has established the city as a top destination for family tourism. Traditional crafts, most notably the exquisite Changzhou combs, continue to be a cherished part of its local identity. Changzhou effectively bridges its legacy as a historic commercial node with its contemporary focus on high-tech innovation.",
